The patch moves the `force_uaccess_begin()` function call back into the `do_exit()` function. This ensures that if a kernel thread has encountered an oops, the address space is correctly reset to `USER_DS` before any further processing occurs. This change prevents unsafe memory access by ensuring that the kernel thread operates in the correct address space, thus maintaining system stability and security.


